# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT
# Leave blank. Vite proxies /api to http://127.0.0.1:8000.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# PUBLIC VERCEL FRONTEND
# In Vercel Project Settings > Environment Variables, set VITE_API_BASE_URL
# to the exact URL of the deployed Clarivo backend, without a trailing slash.
# Example: https://clarivo-api.vercel.app

# OPTIONAL: separate backend for Voice + Visual analysis.
# Point this at a Cloudflare Tunnel to a machine running the OpenVINO stack.
# Content analysis and Q&A keep using VITE_API_BASE_URL, so the site still works
# when that machine is off - only Voice/Visual report unavailable, and they come
# back on their own once it returns.
#
# THIS IS NO LONGER REQUIRED. The address is also accepted at runtime, which is
# what a quick tunnel needs: its hostname changes on every start, and a value
# set here is frozen into the bundle at build time, so it would mean a redeploy
# per session. At runtime the address comes from, highest priority first:
#
#   1. ?ai=https://abc-def.trycloudflare.com  in the link people are given
#   2. what that link stored in the browser, or what was typed into the
#      "Voice + Visual" field in the app header
#   3. this variable
#
# So set this only for an address that does not change - a named tunnel on your
# own domain. Leave it blank for quick tunnels and share the link that
# start-tunnel.bat prints.
#
# Leave blank AND with no runtime address to send everything to
# VITE_API_BASE_URL (the original behaviour).
# See DEPLOY_TUNNEL.md.
VITE_LOCAL_AI_BASE_URL=
